The portable C in the scenario setup-help-screens: what it is expected to show
otherwise than the original. A patch of
harness/goldens/setup-help-screens.txt, see harness/goldens.py: a line with -
is the golden's, a line with + is what is expected in its place.
Deviation: 1, 5, 7 of src/portable_c/DEVIATIONS.md
Why: the Configuration of the setup has no Memory allocation and no TSR
manager: Execute options is one line, Quick execute commands, and the Keyboard
options stand two rows further up, with the last two rows of the right half
empty; and Screen and Mouse of the setup has no Screen output: the Other
options and the Mouse options stand five rows further up, where that group
was, with the right half empty below them, where the line of characters is the
fourth field, three times Tab from the first. Under the help the two boxes
show nothing of their right halves. The mouse pointer exchanges the colours of
the cell that it is on, the middle of the screen where nothing has moved it:
the lines have moved under it, and it stays

